BORRADOR DE E0 (18-oct-2026) — NO APLICADO a ningun arbol. Parche 1/3 de la serie de audio.

arm64: uke-abl: admitir el bus I2C de los amplificadores (i2c@88c000) en uke_abl_transform()

Hoy uke_scope_qup_buses() deja en QUP1 solo i2c@890000/ktz8866@11 y pone status="disabled" al resto, por
lo que el bus i2c-4 de Android (QUP1 SE3, 4x FourSemi FS19xx en 0x34-0x37) llega al kernel apagado.

Cambios (solo uke-abl.c):
  - uke_amp_bus(): validador "fail closed" nuevo, al estilo de uke_backlight_bus(): compat qcom,i2c-geni,
    reg 0x88c000/0x4000, interconnects IGUALES byte a byte a los del bus KTZ (mismo QUP1), interrupcion SPI 585,
    ruta DMA OEM {0,3,3,64,2},{1,3,3,64,2} hacia gpi-dma@800000 (la 5a celda vale 2 aqui y 0 en el KTZ;
    gpi_of_dma_xlate() solo lee las tres primeras), y exactamente cuatro hijos fs19xx_smartpa@34..37 con
    compat foursemi,fs16xx. Cualquier desviacion rechaza el arranque como las demas comprobaciones.
  - uke_scope_qup_buses(): admite i2c@88c000 y sus cuatro hijos (tabla admitted[][5], 4 padres).
  - uke_board_pins(): valida los pines del bus (gpio44 qup1_se3_l0, gpio45 qup1_se3_l1, reposo gpio) y las
    lineas reset-gpio (30/149/124/123) e irq-gpio (47/69/31/129, flags 0x2008) de los cuatro amplificadores.
  - No se admite ningun SMMU nuevo: el bus usa el wrapper QUP1 (0x423) y GPI1 (0x436) ya admitidos.

Verificado en el PC (kernel/harness + live-android-os3.dtb, ver AUDIO-E0-20261018.md §3): con el parche, la salida
de uke_abl_transform() difiere de la original en UNA linea (status del i2c@88c000: "disabled" -> "ok"); 14
mutaciones del DT de entrada (dmas, interconnects, interrupts, reg, reg/compat/gpio de amplificadores, pines,
hijo extra) son rechazadas (-15) y la original las aceptaba. NO probado en la tablet ni compilado como kernel.
Pendiente aguas abajo: que el driver i2c-qcom-geni sondee ese bus (hace falta DMA GPI en SE3) y el driver FS19xx.

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/uke-abl.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/uke-abl.c
@@ -311,22 +311,84 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Smart-amplifier bus. QUP1 SE3 is the OEM i2c-4 (i2c@88c000) with four FourSemi FS19xx
+ * (DEVID 0x2900) at 0x34-0x37. It shares the QUP1 wrapper, GPI1 and NoC route of the KTZ8866
+ * bus above, so no new SMMU stream is admitted. The OEM DMA route carries a fifth cell of 2
+ * (the KTZ bus has 0); gpi_of_dma_xlate() only reads the first three. Fail closed like the
+ * other graph checks: any deviation rejects the Uke boot.
+ */
+static int UKE_INIT uke_amp_bus(const void *fdt)
+{
+	static const char bus[] = "/soc/qcom,qupv3_1_geni_se@8c0000/i2c@88c000";
+	static const char ktz_bus[] = "/soc/qcom,qupv3_1_geni_se@8c0000/i2c@890000";
+	static const unsigned int route[] = { 0, 3, 3, 64, 2, 1, 3, 3, 64, 2 };
+	int node = fdt_path_offset(fdt, bus), ktz = fdt_path_offset(fdt, ktz_bus);
+	int dma = fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/soc/qcom,gpi-dma@800000");
+	int size, other, i, j, amp;
+	unsigned int phandle, seen = 0;
+	const fdt32_t *value, *ktz_icc;
+
+	if (node < 0 || ktz < 0 || dma < 0 || !(phandle = fdt_get_phandle(fdt, dma)) ||
+	    fdt_node_check_compatible(fdt, node, "qcom,i2c-geni") ||
+	    uke_path_reg(fdt, bus, 0x88c000, 0x4000))
+		return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+	/* Same QUP1 core/config/memory interconnect path as the verified KTZ8866 bus. */
+	value = fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "interconnects", &size);
+	ktz_icc = fdt_getprop(fdt, ktz, "interconnects", &other);
+	if (!value || !ktz_icc || size != other || size != (int)(12 * sizeof(*value)) ||
+	    memcmp(value, ktz_icc, size))
+		return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+	value = fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "interrupts", &size);
+	if (!value || size != (int)(3 * sizeof(*value)) || fdt32_to_cpu(value[0]) ||
+	    fdt32_to_cpu(value[1]) != 585 || fdt32_to_cpu(value[2]) != 4)
+		return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+	value = fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "dmas", &size);
+	if (!value || size != (int)(12 * sizeof(*value)))
+		return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+	for (i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+		if (fdt32_to_cpu(value[i * 6]) != phandle)
+			return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+		for (j = 0; j < 5; j++)
+			if (fdt32_to_cpu(value[i * 6 + j + 1]) != route[i * 5 + j])
+				return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+	}
+	fdt_for_each_subnode(amp, fdt, node) {
+		unsigned int address;
+
+		if (strncmp(fdt_get_name(fdt, amp, NULL), "fs19xx_smartpa@", 15) ||
+		    fdt_node_check_compatible(fdt, amp, "foursemi,fs16xx"))
+			return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+		value = fdt_getprop(fdt, amp, "reg", &size);
+		if (!value || size != 4)
+			return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+		address = fdt32_to_cpu(*value);
+		if (address < 0x34 || address > 0x37 || (seen & (1U << (address - 0x34))))
+			return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+		seen |= 1U << (address - 0x34);
+	}
+	return seen == 0xf ? 0 : -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+}
